<h1><span lang="EN-GB">From Viewport</span></h1>
<hr align="left" width="98.974%" size="6" class="whs3">
<p><span lang="EN-GB">This command is accessible from</span> <span lang="EN-GB" class="Path" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Transformations</b></span> <span class="Path" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>&gt; From Viewport</b></span><span lang="EN-GB">.</span></p>
<p class="Description"><span class="Command" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Description:</b></span> The command <span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>From Viewport</b></span> allows the user to define correspondence between the real position and the viewport position of an object in the scene. The name of the new transformation entity is ‘Viewport’,.</p>
<p>In this case the transformation matrix will be created by direct correspondence of the global co-ordinate system (source) &#160;to the viewport (target) &#160;and not by choosing separate correspondent entities.</p>
<p class="Example" style="text-decoration:underline;"><a class="dropspot" href="javascript:kadovTextPopup(this)" id="a1"><span lang="EN-GB" class="dropspot" style="text-decoration:underline;"><u>Scheme</u></span></a></p>
<div class="droptext" id="POPUP289810763" style="display:'none'; x-ss-type:dropdown;">
<table class="TableGrid" style="border-collapse:collapse; border-spacing:5px;" cellspacing="5">
<col>
<tr valign="middle" class="whs4">
<td valign="top" class="whs5">
<p class="Normal" style="text-align:justify;"><img src="Images/image083.gif" width="469px" height="252px" border="0" class="img_whs6" alt=""></p>
</td>
</tr>
</table>
</div>
<p>The viewport co-ordinate system has the following properties:</p>
<ul>
<li class="kadov-p-Cbullet">
<p class="bullet">The X-axis is parallel to the horizontal direction of the viewport and is oriented from left to right,</p>
</li>
<li class="kadov-p-Cbullet">
<p class="bullet">the Y-axis is parallel to the vertical direction of the viewport and is oriented from bottom to top,</p>
</li>
<li class="kadov-p-Cbullet">
<p class="bullet">the Z-axis is orthogonal to the viewport and is oriented towards us.</p>
</li>
<li class="kadov-p-Cbullet">
<p class="bullet">The origin is unpredictable.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p class="Note" id="P1"><span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Note</b></span>: The created transformation matrix is the same as the viewport entity matrix, but their purpose is different. For details see: &#160;<a href="Create_Viewport_Entity.htm">Create Viewport Entity</a></p>
